Z||000012||ChadMan||07-16-2000||06:44 PM||||Wow, Scott, that looks great.  (I haven't been on the Forum all weekend so this is the first I've seen of the wheels on the car)<P>They kind of look like a blend of Formula wheels and Porsche "cookie cutter" wheels from the 944.  Your wheels look a lot more muscular than the stock "hi-tech" 14" wheel.||||reg||1
Z||000013||87ECO5||07-16-2000||08:31 PM||||Bill - yes, I used five coats of clearcoat.  I also made sure the guys doing the balancing put the weights on the back so the clearcoat wouldn't get chipped.<P>Dave - yes, I have all twenty caps.  I had to "borrow" a few from the parts car.<P>Chad - thanks, man.  Hmmm ... they look muscular?  I never noticed that.  The Goodyears that were on it were 195/70R14's.  I put the 215/60R14's from the parts car on.  Maybe that's why ...<P>BTW, for those interested ... the paint I used on the calipers was something our local Pep Boys just got in this weekend.  It's a product called Brake Caliper Paint from Plastikote.  It doesn't require any primer, it's chip-resistant and it comes in four colors (red, yellow, blue and black).<p>[This message has been edited by 87ECO5 (edited 07-17-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000014||Monkeyman||07-17-2000||12:33 PM||||Red, yellow, blue & black.  Hmm...No purple, huh?  I have to find some light purple (lilac?) for mine if I ever get them.||||reg||1
